<section id="Ax1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">Appendix Overview</h2>

</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Derivation of the importance of atomic expert</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide a detailed derivation of the importance measure introduced in equation <a href="#S3.E13" title="In Importance of Atomic experts. ‣ 3.2 Atomic expert Importance Analysis in the Output Space ‣ 3 Method ‣ Heapr: Hessian-based Efficient atomic expert Pruning in Output Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the negative log-likelihood loss <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, whose per-sample gradient with respect to the parameters <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\Theta}\ell=\bm{J}_{k}^{\top}\mathbf{g}_{\mathbf{e}_{k}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑱</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\Theta}\ell=\bm{J}_{k}^{\top}\mathbf{g}_{\mathbf{e}_{k}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{J}_{k}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{J}_{k}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times P}</annotation></semantics></math> is the Jacobian of the atomic expert output <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to its parameters <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{g}_{\mathbf{e}_{k}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{g}_{\mathbf{e}_{k}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is the gradient of the loss with respect to <math id="A1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By definition, the Fisher Information Matrix is</p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\bm{H}}=\bm{F}=\mathbb{E}\big[(\nabla_{\Theta}\ell)(\nabla_{\Theta}\ell)^{\top}\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑯</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>𝑭</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\bm{H}}=\bm{F}=\mathbb{E}\big[(\nabla_{\Theta}\ell)(\nabla_{\Theta}\ell)^{\top}\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">After model convergence, the Jacobian <math id="A1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{J}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{J}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> can be treated as independent <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Martens &amp; Grosse, 2015</a>)</cite>, substituting the expression of <math id="A1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\Theta}\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\Theta}\ell</annotation></semantics></math> gives</p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{F}=\bm{J}_{k}^{\top}\,\mathbb{E}\!\left[\mathbf{g}_{\mathbf{e}_{k}}\mathbf{g}_{\mathbf{e}_{k}}^{\top}\right]\bm{J}_{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑭</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑱</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐠</mi><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{F}=\bm{J}_{k}^{\top}\,\mathbb{E}\!\left[\mathbf{g}_{\mathbf{e}_{k}}\mathbf{g}_{\mathbf{e}_{k}}^{\top}\right]\bm{J}_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Returning to the quadratic optimization problem in the OBS framework:</p>
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\delta\Theta}\ \tfrac{1}{2}\,\delta\Theta^{\top}\bm{F}\,\delta\Theta\quad\text{s.t.}\quad\bm{J}_{k}\delta\Theta+\mathbf{e}_{k}=0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.667em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑭</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>s.t.</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\delta\Theta}\ \tfrac{1}{2}\,\delta\Theta^{\top}\bm{F}\,\delta\Theta\quad\text{s.t.}\quad\bm{J}_{k}\delta\Theta+\mathbf{e}_{k}=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.4" class="ltx_p">we define the auxiliary variable <math id="A1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}=\bm{J}_{k}\delta\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}=\bm{J}_{k}\delta\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>. The constraint becomes <math id="A1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}+\mathbf{e}_{k}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}+\mathbf{e}_{k}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}=-\mathbf{e}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}=-\mathbf{e}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the objective reduces to</p>
<table id="A1.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\mathbf{u}}\ \tfrac{1}{2}\,\mathbf{u}^{\top}\mathbb{E}\!\left[\mathbf{g}_{\mathbf{e}_{k}}\mathbf{g}_{\mathbf{e}_{k}}^{\top}\right]\mathbf{u}\quad\text{s.t.}\quad\mathbf{u}+\mathbf{e}_{k}=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>𝐮</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.667em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐠</mi><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐮</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>s.t.</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\mathbf{u}}\ \tfrac{1}{2}\,\mathbf{u}^{\top}\mathbb{E}\!\left[\mathbf{g}_{\mathbf{e}_{k}}\mathbf{g}_{\mathbf{e}_{k}}^{\top}\right]\mathbf{u}\quad\text{s.t.}\quad\mathbf{u}+\mathbf{e}_{k}=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.5" class="ltx_p">Plugging in the constraint yields the optimal cost:</p>
<table id="A1.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\ell=\tfrac{1}{2}\,\mathbf{e}_{k}^{\top}\,\mathbb{E}\!\left[\mathbf{g}_{\mathbf{e}_{k}}\mathbf{g}_{\mathbf{e}_{k}}^{\top}\right]\mathbf{e}_{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐠</mi><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\ell=\tfrac{1}{2}\,\mathbf{e}_{k}^{\top}\,\mathbb{E}\!\left[\mathbf{g}_{\mathbf{e}_{k}}\mathbf{g}_{\mathbf{e}_{k}}^{\top}\right]\mathbf{e}_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.6" class="ltx_p">We therefore define the importance of the <math id="A1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th atomic expert as</p>
<table id="A1.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\;=\;\tfrac{1}{2}\,\mathbf{e}_{k}^{\top}\,\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbf{g}_{\mathbf{e}_{k}}\mathbf{g}_{\mathbf{e}_{k}}^{\top}\right]\mathbf{e}_{k}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐠</mi><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\;=\;\tfrac{1}{2}\,\mathbf{e}_{k}^{\top}\,\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbf{g}_{\mathbf{e}_{k}}\mathbf{g}_{\mathbf{e}_{k}}^{\top}\right]\mathbf{e}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.7" class="ltx_p">which is a scalar since <math id="A1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}_{k}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}_{k}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{g}_{\mathbf{e}_{k}}\mathbf{g}_{\mathbf{e}_{k}}^{\top}]\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐠</mi><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{g}_{\mathbf{e}_{k}}\mathbf{g}_{\mathbf{e}_{k}}^{\top}]\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This formalizes equation <a href="#S3.E13" title="In Importance of Atomic experts. ‣ 3.2 Atomic expert Importance Analysis in the Output Space ‣ 3 Method ‣ Heapr: Hessian-based Efficient atomic expert Pruning in Output Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> in the main text: the smaller the value of <math id="A1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, the less impact the <math id="A1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th atomic expert has on the overall model loss, making it a better candidate for pruning.</p>
</div>
</section>
</article>
</div>
